Under 29 CFR 1910.132(d)(2), the employer must verify that the workplace hazard assessment was performed through a written certification [1]. 

This written certification must identify:
- The workplace evaluated [1];
- The person certifying that the evaluation was performed [1];
- The date(s) of the hazard assessment [1]; and
- The document itself as a certification of hazard assessment [1].
